 "answer": "The LlamaIndex function that loads a persisted index back from a storage context is `load_index_from_storage`. This function is used in the following contexts:\n\n1. **Loading a Single Index:**\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.core import load_index_from_storage\n   index = load_index_from_storage(storage_context)\n   ```\n\n2. **Loading the RAG Index:**\n   ```python\n   from llama_index.core import StorageContext, load_index_from_storage\n   storage_context = StorageContext.from_defaults(persist_dir=\"storage\")\n   index = load_index_from_storage(storage_context)\n   ```\n\nThese examples illustrate how `load_index_from_storage` is used to retrieve a previously persisted index from a storage context.",
